## QUALITY STANDARDS

### Vocabulary
- Use predominantly high-frequency words for grade {{ grade }}
- Avoid words more than 1 grade level above target
- Include some challenge words appropriate to Lexile range
- Prioritize decodability for oral reading

### Sentence Structure
- Vary sentence length naturally
- Use grade-appropriate syntax
- Avoid overly complex embedded clauses
- Ensure natural prosody opportunities (rhythm, phrasing)

### Content
- Engaging, age-appropriate topic
- Clear narrative flow
- Natural dialogue is acceptable unless prohibited
- Culturally sensitive and inclusive
- Positive themes appropriate for assessment context

### Oral Reading Considerations
- Natural phrase boundaries at punctuation
- Opportunities for expression and intonation
- Manageable multi-syllable words for grade level
- Clear context clues for challenging words

## OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS

Provide ONLY the passage text with:
- No title
- No formatting (bold, italics, etc.)
- No preamble or explanation
- No word count in output (but ensure it meets requirements)
- Natural paragraph breaks (2-4 paragraphs)
- Proper punctuation for oral reading flow

## EXAMPLE STRUCTURE (Grade 2, ~140 words)

Paragraph 1 (50-60 words): Introduce character and setting
Paragraph 2 (40-50 words): Present situation or action
Paragraph 3 (40-50 words): Resolution or conclusion

Remember: This passage is for ORAL READING FLUENCY, not comprehension. Focus on:
- Natural flow for reading aloud
- Appropriate pacing markers (punctuation)
- Grade-level vocabulary and syntax
- Exact word count within ±2 words of {{ target_word_count }}

